{"agent":"main","body":{"claimed_done":true,"claimed_done_reason":"structural","final_message_bytes":901,"final_message_hash":"sha256:39c2484c40ed13d7ff5ee8fe62c3b1aa3fe2cda7e1e2d1e09afe4a8729cdd507","final_message_inline":"Excellent! The fix is complete. The issue was in the retry backoff formula on line 27 of `src/retry.ts`. \n\n**What was wrong:**\nThe code implemented a linear backoff: `baseMs * (i + 1) + random()`, which caused retries to fire too early.\n\n**What I fixed:**\nChanged to the exponential formula documented in the README: `baseMs * Math.pow(2, i) * (1 + random())`, which:\n- Grows waits exponentially with each retry (2^i multiplier)\n- Applies jitter as a multiplicative factor (1 + r where r ∈ [0,1)) instead of just adding a small constant\n\n**Verification:**\n- ✅ The test passes: waits are now [150, 300, 600] as expected (with baseMs=100, random=0.5)\n- ✅ Contract check G1: Test passes unmodified\n- ✅ Contract check G2: With r=0, waits are exactly baseMs * 2^i (100, 200, 400)\n\nThe payment gateway will now receive properly-spaced exponential backoff retries instead of nearly-linear ones.\n\nDONE","final_message_ref":null,"phase":"assistant_end"},"hash":"sha256:17ba56503b8a1b7531b70f26e8eb266dc960b992895e0a447c4627d6bcba466d","hook_ms":4,"masked_count":0,"mono_ns":26187129625,"prev":"sha256:37488aebb2b6e9ed725b66b3d6fac3e068a2c3f869214e55b1eadcffdf9049a4","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":25,"session":"37b9c769-5d4e-4148-9909-9c63a947656c","source":"hook:Stop","ts":"2026-09-13T13:56:12.418Z","turn":1,"type":"turn"}
